From c4ceb5e674099b6244b0c0e6506f9a0298698fba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <vital.had@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:16:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add OpenGL 1 video output module

Fixed-function OpenGL 1.x video writer for the legacy renderer, aimed at
GPUs without OpenGL 2.0 (e.g. G4 Macs on Mac OS X 10.4). It is a separate
module next to QPainter and XVideo, independent of the OpenGL 2 renderer
in libqmplay2, and needs only QtOpenGL (QGLWidget), so it builds with Qt4
and Qt5.

- Optional GLSL fragment shader path (Y/Cb/Cr planes as luminance
  textures, BT.601/BT.709 and limited/full range from the frame,
  brightness/contrast/saturation/hue on the GPU).
- CPU fallback path using swscale to RGB32, GPU only scales/flips/zooms;
  used when shaders are disabled in the module settings or unsupported.
- Power-of-two texture allocation with sub-image uploads when NPOT
  textures are unavailable, no CPU resampling needed.
- Endian-safe BGRA/UNSIGNED_INT_8_8_8_8_REV uploads for RGB and OSD.
- open() fails cleanly without a GL context, so the legacy output list
  falls through to the next module (QPainter).

Enabled with -DUSE_OPENGL1=ON (default OFF). Refused on Qt6 builds,
where QGLWidget no longer exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TT6KirfnBKdTErka33cSUn
